Spiking Neural Network Hardware Accelerator

A Verilog-based hardware implementation of a Spiking Neural Network (SNN) designed for efficient neuromorphic computation and FPGA/ASIC prototyping. This project focuses on building a multilayer SNN architecture with dedicated neuron cores, memory modules, FIFO buffering, layer controllers, and classification logic for applications such as MNIST-style pattern recognition. The repository provides a modular framework for exploring low-power, event-driven neural computation in digital hardware.

Key Features
Hardware implementation of multilayer Spiking Neural Network architecture
Modular Verilog design for neuron cores, hidden layers, and output layer
FIFO-based spike data flow management
Layer-wise control modules for synchronized spike propagation
Weight and input memory blocks for dataset integration
Argmax and spike counter modules for final classification
Designed for FPGA prototyping and neuromorphic accelerator research
Repository Structure

Core modules include:

neuron_core.v – Fundamental spiking neuron processing unit
weights_memory_snn.v – Synaptic weight storage
mnist_input_memory.v – Input sample memory interface
FIFO.v – Spike buffering and synchronization
layer_control_* – Hidden and output layer control modules
argmax.v – Final output decision logic
snn_accelerator_top_3.v – Top-level accelerator integration

